## Pyctuator wiring test

### `test_configure_pyctuator_with_optional_redis_health()`
This is a pure wiring/configuration test.

It replaces:

- `Pyctuator`
- `Redis`
- `RedisHealthProvider`

with fake objects that only record what they receive.

Then it calls `configure_pyctuator(app, settings)`.

It verifies:

- environment provider is registered under `"demo"`
- environment data says Redis health is enabled
- Redis health provider is registered with the correct Redis connection settings
- `app.state.pyctuator` is set

So this proves the app wires Pyctuator correctly when Redis health is enabled.

